  "authoringNotes": {
    "status": "approximate centreline from 2026 OpenStreetMap ways, traced against GSI gazo3 1984–1986 aerials and the 1:25,000 Nara sheet (1983 revision, published 1984-05-30); not surveyed or native-qualified",
    "sprintRoute": "Sanjō-dōri west of the JNR level crossing → JNR Nara Station front → Sanjō-dōri east past Sarusawa-ike and the Kōfuku-ji pagoda → Ichi-no-torii → north past the museum to Kenchō-higashi → Route 369 north → east past Kaidan-in, north beside Daibutsu-ike and the Shōsō-in → Shin-Wakakusayama toll gate → switchbacks via Mikasa Onsen and Jikkoku-dai → Wakakusa-yama summit car park",
    "topologyReason": "A city run into a hill climb with real, distinct endpoints. Sanjō-dōri's station section was eastbound-only and the driveway beyond the summit is a one-way, unpaved forest road, so no legal 1986 loop returns to the start without a fabricated return leg.",
    "oneWay": "Sanjō-dōri 樽井町–国鉄奈良駅前 eastbound only 8:00–21:00 from December 1965 (奈良県公報4473); driven eastbound on a weekday before 21:00. The climb is driven uphill from the north gate, the legal direction whether two-way (today) or one-way north→south (the through course). The one-way unpaved Kasuga Okuyama road beyond the summit is not used.",
    "designations": "Route 369 (designated 1975-04-01) along 登大路 and north from 県庁東, shown in national-road colour on the 1983 map. The Ichi-no-torii–Kenchō-higashi road became Route 169 only on 1993-04-01; show no 169 shield.",
    "elevationsAndWidths": "Elevations from the GSI dem5a laser DEM (modern), smoothed over about ±40 m and limited to 12% per control-point edge; at most about 6 m below the raw DEM near Jikkoku-dai. Half-widths are authored estimates: Sanjō-dōri 3.8–4.4 m (about 8 m wide in 1986), Ichi-no-torii–Route 369 4.6–4.8 m, the Tōdai-ji lane 3.0 m, the driveway 3.3 m, narrowed to 2.7–3.2 m in the tightest hairpins to satisfy the curvature bound.",
    "cornerGeometry": "Quadratic tangent trims in millimetres, not physical radii. City corners use one control point with 12–18 m trims (compiled radii 8.6–13.4 m). On the driveway a control point is placed on the smoothed OSM centreline after about 28° of heading change or 70 m, never closer than 7.5 m, with the maximum trim. Compiled tightest radius 5.8 m against 5.6 m on the OSM centreline.",
    "pacing": "One-dimensional model of the handling constants and the test-driver rule (check.ts): 146.5 s. Run read-only against the repo's generated eight-car AI races, the same model was within 1% of the AI winner on irohazaka-1986 (170.6 against 172.4 s) and kyoto-1986 (198.6 against 201.0 s), and 13% fast on aizu-wakamatsu-1986 (129.2 against 148.3 s). Expect an AI winner of about 150–170 s and a last car of about 160–185 s; targetMs 180000 sits at the slow end. The AI never targets below 850 mm/tick, above the steering limit in the 6–10 m hairpins, so time the field in the driving lab before qualification.",
    "musicCues": "Provisional jo-ha-kyū markers at the modelled arrival times: level crossing start, Ichi-no-torii, toll gate, Mikasa Onsen hairpins, Jikkoku-dai, sky ridge. The asset and digest are placeholders.",
    "notForProfile": "Not in STREET_ROUTE_IDS or the native catalog. This input cannot be submitted to any live profile.",
    "unconfirmed": "1986 public status and direction of the Tōdai-ji lane (大仏殿北・正倉院西); 1986 paving, width and toll of the climb; the 1986 prefectural number of the Ichi-no-torii–Kenchō-higashi road; whether Sanjō-dōri was under community-road works in 1986."
  },
